@page
@model HrSystemDhg.Web.Pages.Admin.RulesModel
@using HrSystemDhg.Web.Services
@{ViewData["Title"]="Attendance & payroll rules"; var dayNames = new[] { "Sunday", "Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday" };}
<div class="eyebrow">MAIN SETTINGS · HR</div>
<h1>Attendance &amp; payroll rules</h1>
<p class="page-intro">Manage work schedules, attendance windows and deduction rates. All times use East Africa Time (UTC+3).</p>
<div class="grid">
<partial name="/Pages/Shared/_RegistrationCsv.cshtml" model='("work rules")' />
<partial name="/Pages/Shared/_RegistrationCsv.cshtml" model='("shifts")' view-data='new ViewDataDictionary(ViewData) { ["CsvDataset"] = "shifts" }' />
<partial name="/Pages/Shared/_RegistrationCsv.cshtml" model='("holidays")' view-data='new ViewDataDictionary(ViewData) { ["CsvDataset"] = "holidays" }' />
</div>
<div asp-validation-summary="All" role="alert"></div>
<form method="post" class="card">
<input type="hidden" name="payrollId" value="@Model.PayrollId" />
<input type="hidden" name="WorkingDaysSubmitted" value="true" />
<h2>1. Effective date and scope</h2>
<p>Save a new version to change a policy. The previous version continues to apply to earlier dates. Rules resolve by shift, department, branch, then global default.</p>
<div class="grid">
<label>Effective from<input asp-for="Rule.EffectiveFrom" type="date" required /></label>
<label>Branch<select asp-for="Rule.BranchId"><option value="">All branches</option>@foreach(var b in Model.Branches){<option value="@b.Id">@b.Name</option>}</select></label>
<label>Department<select asp-for="Rule.DepartmentId"><option value="">All departments</option>@foreach(var d in Model.Departments){<option value="@d.Id">@d.Name</option>}</select></label>
<label>Shift<select asp-for="Rule.ShiftId"><option value="">All shifts</option>@foreach(var shift in Model.Shifts){<option value="@shift.Id">@shift.Name</option>}</select></label>
</div>
<hr /><h2>2. Working days and required hours</h2>
<div class="actions" role="group" aria-label="Working days">@foreach(var number in new[] {6,0,1,2,3,4,5}){
<label class="inline"><input type="checkbox" name="WorkingDays" value="@number" checked="@Model.WorkingDays.Contains(number)" /> @dayNames[number]</label>
}</div>
<div class="grid">
<label>Required work hours per day<input asp-for="Rule.DailyHours" type="number" min="0.25" max="20" step="0.25" required /></label>
<label>Unpaid break minutes<input asp-for="Rule.BreakMinutes" type="number" min="0" max="180" required /></label>
</div>
<p>Worked minutes = time out − time in − unpaid break. Approved leave reduces required attendance minutes. Non-working days and holidays have no attendance deduction.</p>
<hr /><h2>3. Check-in and checkout windows</h2>
<label class="inline"><input asp-for="Rule.UsePunchWindows" /> Use attendance windows and deduct minutes short of the daily requirement</label>
<div class="grid">
<label>Check-in opens (EAT)<input name="Rule.CheckInFrom" type="time" value='@Model.Rule.CheckInFrom.ToString(@"hh\:mm")' required /></label>
<label>Check-in closes (EAT)<input name="Rule.CheckInUntil" type="time" value='@Model.Rule.CheckInUntil.ToString(@"hh\:mm")' required /></label>
<label>Checkout opens (EAT)<input name="Rule.CheckOutFrom" type="time" value='@Model.Rule.CheckOutFrom.ToString(@"hh\:mm")' required /></label>
<label>Checkout closes (EAT)<input name="Rule.CheckOutUntil" type="time" value='@Model.Rule.CheckOutUntil.ToString(@"hh\:mm")' required /></label>
</div>
<p>Punches outside the windows remain in the raw log. A missing valid check-in or checkout follows the incomplete-punch policy below.</p>
<hr /><h2>4. Deduction formula and rate</h2>
<div class="grid">
<label>Calculation method<select asp-for="Rule.MinuteRateMode"><option value="Salary">Monthly basic salary ÷ salary days ÷ daily minutes</option><option value="Fixed">Fixed amount per missing minute</option></select></label>
<label>Salary days divisor (attendance and unpaid leave)<input asp-for="Rule.SalaryDivisor" type="number" min="1" max="366" step="1" required /></label>
<label>Fixed rate per minute (employee salary currency)<input asp-for="Rule.FixedMinuteRate" type="number" min="0" step="0.000001" required /></label>
<label>Missing check-in or checkout<select asp-for="Rule.IncompletePolicy"><option value="Flag">Require HR review before payroll</option><option value="Absent">Deduct the unexcused full day</option><option value="Half day">Deduct up to half a day</option></select></label>
</div>
<div class="notice" id="formula-preview" aria-live="polite">@AttendanceMinutes.Formula(Model.Rule) × missing minutes</div>
<p>A full absence uses the same rate for the daily required minutes. Approved paid leave has no salary deduction. Approved unpaid leave is deducted separately using basic salary ÷ salary days divisor × approved leave fraction; it is excluded from absence counts and attendance penalties. Attendance waivers do not waive unpaid leave.</p>
<details><summary>Fixed-shift and overtime settings</summary><div class="grid">
<label>Fixed shift start hour<input asp-for="Rule.StartHour" type="number" min="0" max="23" /></label>
<label>Fixed shift start minute<input asp-for="Rule.StartMinute" type="number" min="0" max="59" /></label>
<label>Fixed shift grace minutes<input asp-for="Rule.GraceMinutes" type="number" min="0" /></label>
<label>Fixed shift absence multiplier<input asp-for="Absence" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" /></label>
<input asp-for="Late" type="hidden" />
<label>Approved overtime multiplier<input asp-for="Rule.OvertimeMultiplier" type="number" min="0" step="0.1" /></label>
<label class="inline"><input asp-for="Rule.WeekendOvertime" /> Allow approved overtime on non-working days</label>
</div></details>
<div class="actions"><button>Save new effective version</button><a class="button secondary" href="/Admin/Settings">Main settings</a></div>
</form>
<section class="card table-scroll"><h2>Policy versions</h2>
<table class="workspace-table"><thead><tr><th>Effective</th><th>Scope</th><th>Working days</th><th>Hours / break</th><th>Check-in / checkout (EAT)</th><th>Deduction</th><th>Manage</th></tr></thead><tbody>
@foreach(var r in Model.Rules){<tr>
<td>@r.EffectiveFrom.ToString("dd MMM yyyy")</td>
<td>@(Model.Branches.FirstOrDefault(x=>x.Id==r.BranchId)?.Name ?? "All branches") · @(Model.Departments.FirstOrDefault(x=>x.Id==r.DepartmentId)?.Name ?? "All departments") · @(Model.Shifts.FirstOrDefault(x=>x.Id==r.ShiftId)?.Name ?? "All shifts")</td>
<td>@string.Join(", ", r.WorkingWeekdays.Split(',').Select(n=>dayNames[int.Parse(n)]))</td>
<td>@r.DailyHours hours / @r.BreakMinutes min</td>
<td>@if(r.UsePunchWindows){<span>@r.CheckInFrom.ToString(@"hh\:mm")–@r.CheckInUntil.ToString(@"hh\:mm")<br />@r.CheckOutFrom.ToString(@"hh\:mm")–@r.CheckOutUntil.ToString(@"hh\:mm")</span>}else{<span>Fixed shift @r.StartHour:@r.StartMinute.ToString("00")</span>}</td>
<td>@(r.UsePunchWindows ? AttendanceMinutes.Formula(r) : "Fixed shift late / early minutes")</td>
<td><a asp-route-templateId="@r.Id">Change this rule</a></td>
</tr>}
</tbody></table></section>
<div class="grid">
<form method="post" asp-page-handler="Shift" class="card"><h2>Add shift</h2><label>Name<input name="name" required /></label><button>Create shift</button></form>
<form method="post" asp-page-handler="Holiday" class="card"><h2>Add public holiday</h2><label>Name<input name="name" required /></label><label>Date<input name="date" type="date" required /></label><label>Branch<select name="branchId"><option value="">All branches</option>@foreach(var b in Model.Branches){<option value="@b.Id">@b.Name</option>}</select></label><button>Add holiday</button></form>
</div>
<section class="card"><h2>Public holidays</h2>@foreach(var h in Model.Holidays){<form method="post" asp-page-handler="RemoveHoliday" class="inline"><input type="hidden" name="id" value="@h.Id"/><span>@h.Date.ToString("dd MMM yyyy") · @h.Name</span><button>Remove holiday</button></form>}</section>
<script>
(() => {
 const field = n => document.querySelector('[name="Rule.' + n + '"]');
 const preview = () => { const hours = Number(field('DailyHours').value); const days = Number(field('SalaryDivisor').value); document.getElementById('formula-preview').textContent = field('MinuteRateMode').value === 'Fixed' ? field('FixedMinuteRate').value + ' per minute × missing minutes' : 'Monthly basic salary ÷ ' + days + ' days ÷ ' + Math.round(hours * 60) + ' minutes × missing minutes'; };
 ['DailyHours','SalaryDivisor','MinuteRateMode','FixedMinuteRate'].forEach(n=>field(n).addEventListener('input',preview)); preview();
})();
</script>
